Z||000000||KnightRyder31||04-28-2000||02:09 PM||||When I'm accelerating hard, and my trans is about to shift at about 5100RPM it makes a wierd gurgeling noise. What is that?||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||04-28-2000||05:06 PM||||have you checked the fluid?  Make sure it's a pretty pink color, and not brownish or burnt-smelling.  Is the fluid at the proper level?  Make sure you're checking it while the car is running.  Has the tranny ever been serviced(new fluid and filter?)  Also make sure the TV cable is adjusted properly.  You may want to get a shop manual for this....  It's really not a big deal to change fluid and filter.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||KnightRyder31||04-29-2000||10:27 AM||||Ok, heres some quick info about my car. I just bought it about a month ago, so I dont know much about it. It's a 84' auto with only 64,000 miles on it! The car itself is in near mint cond. I payed $2,300 for it....including tax and plates, ect. Anyways, your saying that noise I'm hearing should not be there? Oh one more thing, is there anything I could do to make the 4cyl have more power, or some how increase the speed and acceleration? I'm thinking about buying a Borla exhaust system in the summer....would that help any? If you have any sugestions, please tell me.<BR>-----Knight-----<p>[This message has been edited by KnightRyder31 (edited 04-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||04-29-2000||11:00 AM||||It's a 4 cylinder 92 hp engine for God's sake, with an automatic transmission no less.  Nothing that you can do to that combination  will make the car win the national drag race championship.  If anything it would probably do  well on a road course or on slalum racing, but off the line acceleration .....<P>Enjoy the car for what it is.||||reg||1
