Z||000007||Ozzy||04-30-2000||12:27 AM||||Yup...Actually if you are getting it to 5000 rpm clean, especially with the auto tranny, you are doing pretty good dude. My Coupe took a lot of fixing, tweaking etc to get it to do THAT and It is a 5 speed. The 4 cyl (Iron Puke) does not like that kinda treatment much. I can hear my crank begin to rattle over 5 grand. But having asked this same question myself along with every other new 4cyl Fiero owner that ever existed, I agree with the guys...do the basic mods, get it running clean and luv it for what it is. If you want the extra HUTZVA, buy a Fiero with a V-6! (Damn, listen to me...do you older members remember when I first came along?) I did and also kept the 4 banger. Runs nice  now and gets excellent gas mileage. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ozzy||||reg||1
